Validation failed for tool "submit_decision":
  - actions_claimed: must have required properties actions_claimed

Received arguments:
{
  "case_state": "R-4799 (boiler pressure, routine, heating) is at double_quotation stage. £780 quote (expansion vessel) is above the landlord's £250 routine limit; landlord asked for a second quote. Swift P&H visit booked 2026-10-14 per ticket history. Waiting on second quote and landlord decision.",
  "next_actions": [
    {
      "action": "Replied to Jonah Okafor by email with boiler status, what happens next, gas emergency line, and council bin guidance",
      "ledger_id": "A1",
      "type": "REPLY_TO_TENANT",
      "recipient": "Jonah Okafor, tenant",
      "channel": "email"
    }
  ],
  "boundaries": [
    "The 14 Oct visit date comes from the ticket history; not independently confirmed with Swift P&H",
    "Second quote is not yet received, so no cost is approved",
    "Bin collection schedule is held by Tower Hamlets Council; not verified by us"
  ],
  "remaining_work": [
    "Obtain Swift P&H second quote after 14 Oct visit (owner: operations)",
    "Send both quotes to Margaret Ellison for approval, as the £780 quote exceeds her £250 routine limit (owner: operations)"
  ],
  "missing_info": [
    "Confirmation that the Swift P&H visit on 2026-10-14 is booked with the contractor"
  ],
  "outcome": "action_taken",
  "severity": "routine",
  "summary": "Jonah asked for an update on his boiler job and when bins are collected. I replied by email (ledger A1) explaining that R-4799 is awaiting a second quote after the £780 repair exceeded the landlord's £250 limit, with a Swift P&H visit on 14 October, and directed the bin question to Tower Hamlets Council. No new tickets were created because the boiler issue is already open and the bin collection is a council matter.",
  "answers": [
    {
      "question": "What is the current status of his boiler job and what does it mean for him?",
      "answer": "R-4799 is at double_quotation. The £780 expansion-vessel quote is over the landlord's £250 routine limit, so a second quote was requested; Swift P&H is due 2026-10-14. For him: it is routine, not an emergency, and the work will wait for the second quote and the landlord's decision before it goes ahead. He was told what to do if the boiler fails or he smells gas."
    },
    {
      "question": "How do you handle the bin question?",
      "answer": "Not a repair. Bin collection is run by Tower Hamlets Council, so I directed him to the council (website or phone) and did not create a ticket. He was told we do not hold the collection schedule."
    },
    {
      "question": "Do you create any new tickets?",
      "answer": "No. The boiler issue is already open as R-4799, so a new ticket would be a duplicate, and the bin issue belongs to the council."
    }
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Email is the right channel because the tenant prefers email; the portal reply was sent by email to the address on file",
    "Tenant is vulnerable (anxiety), so the reply was kept clear and calm"
  ],
  "conflicts": [],
  "failed_actions": []
}

